{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyLifting","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.HomotopyGroupFunctor"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.Prod.homotopyGroupMap_fst_eq_const_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.Prod.homotopyGroupMap_fst_eq_const_iff","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L238-L253","doc":"**The hypothesis is not vacuous.** For the projection of a trivial bundle\nthe relative lifting property is a theorem, so exactness at the middle spot\nholds unconditionally there.\n\nA trivial bundle is the case where nothing needs lifting theory: the lift\nis written down. Recorded not because the conclusion is interesting there\nbut because it is the witness that the hypothesis of the general theorem is\nsatisfiable at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.pi_range_eq_ker","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.pi_range_eq_ker","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L221-L230","doc":"**Exactness at `π_{n+1}(E, e)`**, spelled with `Fin (n + 1)` so that it is\nliterally a statement about `π_{n+1}`. `Fin (n + 1)` supplies both\n`DecidableEq` and `Nonempty`, which is exactly why the shift by one is\nthere and not an off-by-one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.pi_eq_homotopyGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.pi_eq_homotopyGroup","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L215-L219","doc":"`π_n` in Mathlib's `HomotopyGroup.Pi` spelling is the `Fin n`-indexed\nhomotopy group, definitionally. Recorded so the results above are visibly\nabout `π_n` and not about some neighbouring object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.injective_homotopyGroupHom_of_subsingleton_fibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.injective_homotopyGroupHom_of_subsingleton_fibre","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L193-L207","doc":"**A vanishing fibre group makes `p_*` injective.**\n\nThis is `QOU.Mathlib.LongExactSequence.injective_iff_prev_eq_zero` in its\ntopological habitat, and it is the reason exactness at one spot is worth\nhaving on its own: injectivity of `p_*` is not a fact about `p_*`, it is a\nfact about `π_N(F)`. Nothing else in the sequence is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.range_homotopyGroupHom_eq_ker","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.range_homotopyGroupHom_eq_ker","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L178-L191","doc":"**Exactness at `π_N(E, e)` as `range = ker`.**\n\nThe same theorem as `homotopyGroupMap_eq_const_iff`, phrased the way an\nexact sequence is normally quoted. It needs `Nonempty N` only because that\nis when `π_N` is a group at all — no extra topology is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.homotopyGroupMap_eq_const_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.homotopyGroupMap_eq_const_iff","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L153-L170","doc":"**Exactness at `π_N(E, e)`**, as pointed sets.\n\nStated with `⟦GenLoop.const⟧` rather than `1` on purpose: the identity is\ntrue for every index type `N`, including empty and singleton ones where\nMathlib's group structure is unavailable. `range_homotopyGroupHom_eq_ker`\nbelow is the group-theoretic reading, and it is strictly less general. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.exists_preimage_of_map_eq_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.exists_preimage_of_map_eq_const","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L118-L151","doc":"**The other half, and the place the fibration hypothesis is spent.**\n\nIf `p_* ⟦g⟧` is trivial, then `g` is homotopic rel `∂Iᴺ` to a cube that\nlands in the fibre. Lift the nullhomotopy of `p ∘ g`; its endpoint lands in\n`F` because the homotopy ended at `b`, and it is *based* because the lift\nwas chosen not to move on `∂Iᴺ`. The lifted homotopy is itself the homotopy\nexhibiting the two classes as equal — no second construction is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.fibre_comp_eq_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.fibre_comp_eq_const","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L106-L116","doc":"**Half of exactness, with no hypothesis.** The composite\n`π_N(F) → π_N(E) → π_N(B)` is trivial, because `p ∘ ι` is constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.comp_fibreIncl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.comp_fibreIncl","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L95-L100","doc":"`p` restricted to the fibre is constant. This is the definition of the\nfibre read as an equation between continuous maps, and it is the only\ningredient in the easy half of exactness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.fibreIncl_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.fibreIncl_apply","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L92-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.fibreIncl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.fibreIncl","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L89-L90","doc":"**The inclusion of the fibre**, `F ↪ E`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.mem_fibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.mem_fibre","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.Fibre","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FibrationExactness.Fibre","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FibrationExactness.lean#L84-L85","doc":"**The fibre** of `p` over `b`, as a subspace of `E`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}